{"accepted_at":"2026-09-05T03:22:24Z","case":{"argument_date":"2021-04-27T00:00:00Z","arguments":[{"argument_date":"2021-04-27T00:00:00Z","heading":"What happened at the argument","official_detail_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcript/2020","official_transcript_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2020/20-472_bp7c.pdf","paragraphs":["Mr. Michel argued the statutory language is straightforward. He stated a small refinery can obtain an extension from the EPA.","Mr. Keisler stated the statute authorizes individual refineries to seek extensions based on hardship.","Mr. Morrison argued the ordinary meaning of extension is to lengthen or prolong. He stated this is the only plausible meaning in this context."],"reargument":false,"sequence":1,"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 10, lines 21-27","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2020/20-472_bp7c.pdf","page_label":"file page 10, lines 21-27"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 11, lines 51-17","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2020/20-472_bp7c.pdf","page_label":"file page 11, lines 51-17"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 11, lines 7-23","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2020/20-472_bp7c.pdf","page_label":"file page 11, lines 7-23"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 13, lines 39-43","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2020/20-472_bp7c.pdf","page_label":"file page 13, lines 39-43"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 14, lines 47-23","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2020/20-4